SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE

The MIT license above applies to the original configuration in this
repository: init.lua, everything under lua/, after/, scripts/, tests/ and
docs/, and the generated files doc/nvim-config.txt and docs/_generated/.

It does NOT apply to the third-party Neovim plugins vendored under
pack/vendor/, which are redistributed unmodified, each under its own
license, and each retaining its own copyright and LICENSE file inside its
directory. Those licenses are not all MIT -- several are Apache-2.0 and
three are GPL-3.0. See docs/_generated/third-party-licenses.md (generated
by scripts/generate-docs.lua, so it cannot go stale) for the current
per-plugin inventory, and the LICENSE file inside each plugin's own
directory for the authoritative text.

Vendoring these plugins is mere aggregation: each plugin remains a
separate work, distributed under its own terms, and this configuration
calls their public APIs rather than incorporating their code. Nothing
here is legal advice -- if you plan to redistribute this repository under
different terms, read the individual licenses yourself.
